WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.647
Let's get a model talking to the app that costs nothing — a local model through Ollama.

2
00:00:03.647 --> 00:00:07.000
This is the perfect way to try everything in the course before you spend a cent.

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.895
First, install Ollama from its site.

4
00:00:08.895 --> 00:00:13.737
Then pull a model — I'll use qwen3 here — and make sure Ollama is running in the background.

5
00:00:13.737 --> 00:00:17.000
On most systems it starts serving automatically after install.

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.333
Now open the app, go to Settings, then Providers.

7
00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:26.048
HarnessStation ships with an Ollama provider already listed, and it auto-detects the server running on localhost port eleven-four-three-four.

8
00:00:26.048 --> 00:00:28.000
If it's found, you'll see it right there.

9
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:38.000
If for some reason it isn't detected, add it by hand: the base URL is http://localhost:11434/v1, and you leave the API key blank — a local server needs no key.

10
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.681
Press Save, then hit Fetch models.

11
00:00:39.681 --> 00:00:45.368
The app asks Ollama what you've got installed and fills in the list — you should see qwen3, the one we just pulled.

12
00:00:45.368 --> 00:00:47.000
That's it: a working, free model.

13
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:47.495
One aside.

14
00:00:47.495 --> 00:00:50.667
If you prefer a graphical app, LM Studio is a great alternative.

15
00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:55.275
Same idea — but its server isn't on by default: you start it manually from the Developer tab.

16
00:00:55.275 --> 00:00:58.000
Once it's serving, you connect it exactly the same way.

17
00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.105
Free and local is one route.

18
00:00:59.105 --> 00:01:04.000
Next we do the other one: connecting a cloud provider with your own API key — and I'll show you exactly where that key goes.

